```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    char src[] = "Hello, World!";
    char dest[10];

    // Using strncpy() to prevent buffer overflow
    strncpy(dest, src, sizeof(dest) - 1);
    dest[sizeof(dest) - 1] = '\0'; // Ensure null-termination

    printf("Destination: %s\n", dest);

    // Implementing length checking
    if (strlen(src) > sizeof(dest) - 1) {
        printf("Error: Source string too long for destination buffer\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```
In this example, we use `strncpy()` to copy the source string `src` to the destination buffer `dest`. We also ensure that the destination buffer is null-terminated by adding a `\0` character at the end. Additionally, we implement length checking by verifying that the length of the source string is within the bounds of the destination buffer.

